A write frees an owned node as soon as a split or rebuild replaces it,
before the root reaches the replacement: an allocation failing between a
split and make_root leaves the root on a freed node, which dropping the
transient frees again. Caught under ASan only: elsewhere the pool takes the
second free without a report (#583).
Guarded-by: "alloc sweep: a transient whose write fails partway is freed once"

diff --git a/bytecaskdb/btree.cppm b/bytecaskdb/btree.cppm
index 974e63e..9b652af 100644
--- a/bytecaskdb/btree.cppm
+++ b/bytecaskdb/btree.cppm
@@ -771,7 +771,7 @@ public:
   // once the root no longer reaches it; a foreign one is retired.
   void discard(N *n) {
     if (owns(n)) {
-      replaced_.push_back(n);
+      N::destroy(n);
       return;
     }
     retired_.push_back(n);
